# No production deploys (unlock: lendwave)

**Default for every agent session.** Production Neon and Vercel prod stay untouched until the team explicitly approves cutover.

## Unlock word

**`lendwave`** — user must type this in the **same message** that asks you to run or recommend a blocked production operation.

Without **`lendwave`** in that user message:

- **Do not run** blocked commands.
- **Do not recommend** blocked commands as the next step.
- **Do not** offer prod deploy as an optional follow-up unless already unlocked.

When the user **has** said **`lendwave`**:

- Run **only** the specific prod operation they asked for.
- Include **`lendwave`** in the shell command string (e.g. `LENDWAVE=lendwave vercel --prod`).
- Remind them to backup first (`bun run backup:neon`).

## Blocked without unlock

| Pattern | Examples |
| ------- | -------- |
| Vercel production | `vercel --prod`, `vercel deploy --prod` |
| Schema push to hosted DB | `db:push`, `drizzle-kit push` against `neon.tech` / prod `DATABASE_URL` |
| Destructive Neon | `neonctl branches delete`, `branches reset`, `projects delete` |
| Remote SQL | Mutating SQL against prod connection strings |

## Allowed without unlock

| Safe | Examples |
| ---- | -------- |
| Local dev | `cd new-app && bun run dev`, `vite dev` |
| Migrations (generate/migrate) | `db:generate`, `db:migrate`, `drizzle-kit migrate` |
| Studio | `db:studio` |
| Backups | `backup:neon`, `backup:neon:branches`, `pg_dump` |
| Read-only | `neonctl branches list`, Neon MCP read queries on dev branch |

## Migration context

During SvelteKit migration, `.env.local` must use **`dev-sveltekit-migration`** Neon branch, never prod. See `docs/archive/operations/pre-migration-backup.md`.

## Shell hooks

`.cursor/hooks/guard-shell.sh` sources `scripts/dev/prod-deploy-guard-lib.sh` — hooks are the backstop.
